# Case Discussion Approach

| Interview Stage | What to expect? | Skills Tested |
| :--- | :--- | :--- |
| Case Interview Question | • Interviewer shares the **case statement**, restate to confirm alignment<br>• Clarify the **business objective**, target metric, and constraints upfront<br>• Identify **case type** (profitability, growth etc.) to guide your approach | • Active listening<br>• Comprehension & synthesis<br>• Business context understanding |
| Developing the structure | • Request a moment to **organize your thoughts** before answering<br>• Build a **MECE framework** that covers all possible drivers logically<br>• Explain your structure clearly, navigate the problem **step-by-step** | • Structured thinking<br>• Logical reasoning<br>• Communication clarity |
| Case Analysis | • Prioritize key branches, use **80/20 rule** & eliminate low-impact areas<br>• Ask for data & **refine hypotheses** as you progress through the case<br>• Be comfortable with **number crunching**, estimations & sanity checks | • Problem solving<br>• Analytical thinking<br>• Data interpretation |
| Summary / Recommendation | • Deliver a **clear, concise recommendation** based on your findings<br>• Back up your suggestion with **2–3 supporting** insights/assumptions<br>• Break down recommendations into **short** and **long-term actions** | • Insight synthesis<br>• Strategic thinking<br>• Clarity and conciseness |
| Questions for Interviewer | • Ask a question that **shows curiosity** about the firm's work or culture<br>• Avoid generic queries—tailor it to the **firm, interviewer, or case**<br>• Use it as a chance to **demonstrate interest** and consulting mindset | • Consulting mindset<br>• Cultural alignment<br>• Curiosity and engagement |

